      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right, the platform LPA handles removable eUICCs fine in general, and I dropped that claim. What breaks here is narrower: EuiccGoogle relies on the eSIM slot the device declares through EuiccPolicy\u0027s sim-slot-mappings (e.g. https://github.com/LineageOS/android_hardware_sony/blob/lineage-23.2/packages/Euicc/res/values/strings.xml). On devices that hand that slot over to a SIM tray through a vendor mechanism, the declaration stops matching the hardware while the slot is handed over, and the system LPA ends up operating on the removable card in a slot declared as a pSIM slot. That is why it misbehaves here while removable eUICCs work fine elsewhere. The description is updated in PS3.",
      "parentUuid": "57043fe7_80387f5d",
